   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 420 of the laws of 1998, relating to the creation of the Piermont library district, in relation to the polling place and hours of voting for library elections",
    "basePrintNo": "S5640",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5640-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 420 of 1998",
    "lawSection": "Villages",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5640\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend chapter 420 of the laws of 1998, relating to the creation of\nthe Piermont library district, in relation to the polling place and\nhours of voting for library elections\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nTo change the polling place of the\nLibrary Elections to the Dennis P. McHugh Piermont Public Library,\nand extend the. hours of voting to between 11:00 a.m. until 8:30 p.m.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nTo Amend Subdivision 2 of Section 2 of\nchapter 420 of the Laws of 1998 to read:\n\nThe polling place for the annual election shall be the Dennis P.\nMcHugh Piermont Public library, and the polls shall remain open from\n11:00 a.m. until 8:30 p.m.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThe adjusted voting hours and changed venue better\nreflect the community's voting patterns. The hours will allow the\nlibrary board to provide the proper supervision within their budget.\nChanging the library election polling place from the Piermont Village\nHall TO the actual library will provide more parking which will be\nhandicapped accessible. The library has many more parking spaces than\nthe previous venue. Because this new arrangement is far more\nconvenient than the previous one, the Board expects an increased\nvoter turnout.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nTo be determined.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediate.\n\n",
